# .dockerignore — what `docker build .` may send to the Docker daemon
#
# The "build context" is every file under the directory given to
# `docker build`, uploaded to the daemon BEFORE the Dockerfile runs. This
# tree can hold several build directories (build-release/, build-debug/,
# each with ~1 GB of _deps), screenshots and probe output, so sending it all
# would make every `docker build` slow for nothing.
#
# The image needs only three files (the Dockerfile COPYs nothing else: the
# source itself is MOUNTED at run time, not baked in). So this is an
# ALLOW-LIST: exclude everything, then re-include exactly what's used.
# New files, build dirs or secrets in the tree can then never leak into the
# context by accident.
*
!cmake/DependencyPins.cmake
!cmake/Prefetch.cmake
!docker/entrypoint.sh
